# J. ASSESSMENTS AND POLICY COMPOSITION

## PM-ASSESS-001 — AssessmentEnvelope

Every authoritative derived assessment carries authority/epoch, subject/scope, input revision set/digest, result, closure/completeness, freshness/expiry, stable reasons, disclosure classification, and limitations.

## PM-ASSESS-002 — Assessment Completeness

At minimum: `COMPLETE_FOR_DECLARED_SCOPE`, `PARTIAL`, `UNKNOWN`. Downstream safety logic does not treat PARTIAL as complete.

## PM-IMPACT-001 — ImpactAssessment

Includes affected targets, dependency/shared-infrastructure effects, target-set effects, control-session/path effects, disconnects, state/data-loss possibility, persistence, reversibility/compensation, and UNKNOWN consequences.

## PM-PROT-001 — ProtectionAssessment

Protection is effect/action, context, and target-set specific.

## PM-PROT-002 — Conjunctive Protection

All applicable protection constraints must be satisfied. UI severity is only a summary.

## PM-PROT-003 — Protection Classes

Possible summary classes include `NONE`, `CAUTION`, `ELEVATED`, `CRITICAL`, `ABSOLUTE`, `RECOVERY_ONLY`, `UNKNOWN`. UNKNOWN never means NONE.

## PM-PROT-004 — Contextual Protection

Protection may change with topology/state, such as sole control interface, sole Provider, current Core, transition authority, essential compositor/input.

## PM-PROT-005 — Aggregate Protection

Individually safe targets can be unsafe as a set.

## PM-PROT-006 — Protection Override

Every constraint declares whether it is ordinary-overridable, stronger-assurance-overridable, specific-authority-only, Recovery-only, or absolute through ordinary Manager/Core admission.

## PM-PROT-007 — Distributed Commit Protection

Remote/provider effects that require commit-time dynamic protection must use a short-lived/fenced safety lease or explicit commit revalidation. If the executor cannot satisfy the required rule, mutation is unavailable.

## PM-RISK-001 — RiskAssessment

Prime-owned risk can classify `ROUTINE`, `DISRUPTIVE`, `DESTRUCTIVE`, `CRITICAL`, `UNKNOWN` or equivalent. Risk is not permission.

## PM-COMPAT-001 — CompatibilityAssessment

Compatibility is authority-owned and scoped to capability/Provider/Profile/workload/schema/operation. Possible results include `COMPATIBLE`, `PARTIAL`, `INCOMPATIBLE`, `UNKNOWN`.

## PM-HEALTH-001 — Health/Readiness Authority

Lifecycle and health/readiness are separate. Health/readiness comes from the authoritative domain capability or remains UNKNOWN. Manager never derives HEALTHY from RUNNING, low CPU, or no recent error.

## PM-AVAIL-001 — ActionAvailabilityAssessment

Per effect/action kind + target/context. Possible states include `AVAILABLE`, `REQUIRES_PREFLIGHT`, `REQUIRES_STEP_UP`, `REQUIRES_ACTIVATION`, `EXPERIMENTAL_ONLY`, `UNAVAILABLE`, `UNSUPPORTED`, `UNKNOWN`.

## PM-AVAIL-002 — Cheap Availability

Inventory rendering does not run expensive full safety analysis or wake dormant machinery simply to color a button. Cheap summary may return `REQUIRES_PREFLIGHT` or `REQUIRES_ACTIVATION`.

## PM-POLICY-001 — Conservative Policy Composition

Applicable mandatory constraints compose conservatively. Generic “most specific wins” cannot weaken higher authority. Lower authority may tighten. Broadening requires explicitly typed override authority.

## PM-POLICY-002 — Admission Obligation Set

Every candidate effect generates all applicable mandatory contract/policy/context obligation instances. UI may deduplicate presentation; Core admission cannot erase multiplicity.

