# L. DEVELOPER/TEST AND PRODUCTION SUPPORT

## PM-DEV-001 — Developer/Test Authority

Explicit Prime security state with principal/session scope, allowed operation classes, expiry, revocation, audit, and proof purpose.

## PM-DEV-002 — Eligibility Only

Developer/Test authority can make an experimental path eligible for proof. It never bypasses identity, protection, assurance, disclosure, evidence, audit, or Provider fencing.

## PM-DEV-003 — Same Production Path

PM1.5 proof exercises the same Core/Provider implementation intended for production support; a separate test-only path cannot qualify production behavior.

## PM-SUPPORT-001 — Release Support Trust

Production support claims are authenticated by Prime release/support trust, not self-asserted by Provider or renderer.

## PM-SUPPORT-002 — Operation-Scoped Support

Inventory, telemetry, mutation, and other operation scopes are independently supportable.

## PM-SUPPORT-003 — Support Claim

Contains claim identity, operation scope, implementation version, required contract generation, proof references/scopes/preconditions, validity/offline semantics, signer/key epoch, and revocation state.

## PM-SUPPORT-004 — Support Claim Lifecycle

Support claim status has issue/active/expired/revoked/superseded semantics. Terminal states do not reopen.

## PM-SUPPORT-005 — SupportAssessment

Core combines the authenticated claim with the exact mechanically observed dependency set required by the claim, including security continuity and Provider trust, to derive `PRODUCTION_SUPPORTED`, `EXPERIMENTAL`, `UNPROVEN`, `REVOKED`, `UNSUPPORTED`, or `UNKNOWN`.

## PM-SUPPORT-006 — Revocation Timing

Revocation affects future admission once learned. Historical evidence preserves the support state used at original admission. Already-committed effects are not rewritten.

## PM-SUPPORT-007 — Offline Validity

High-risk offline Hosts do not trust cached support claims indefinitely.

## PM-SUPPORT-008 — Historical Key Verification

Support-signing key rotation preserves historical verification while old keys cannot issue new current authority.

