## PM-PROJ-001 — Projection Operations

`UPSERT`, `RETRACT`, `RESET`.

## PM-PROJ-002 — Projection Instance

Carries instance ID, ordered delivery sequence, source/schema generation, disclosure context, and query specification. Frames from old instances are discarded.

## PM-PROJ-003 — Projection Lifecycle

Creation, active delivery, RESET/expiry/termination are explicit. Terminal projection instance never resurrects.

## PM-PROJ-004 — Gap-Free Snapshot/Continuation Join

Initial snapshot and continuation point share one race-free logical boundary or equivalent mechanism proving no unobservable gap.

## PM-PROJ-005 — RETRACT Semantics

RETRACT means no longer in the current authorized projection. It does not assert lifecycle death.

## PM-PROJ-006 — RESET Semantics

RESET applies on relevant disclosure/session/Host/rebind/security/source/schema/control-state discontinuity.

## PM-PROJ-007 — Scope / Closure / Freshness / Truncation Axes

These remain separate. `FILTERED_BY_POLICY` is not the same as `PARTIAL_SOURCE`.

